{
  "dom_id": "step-q7541",
  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Find the $y$-intercepts of the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=64.$",
  "worked_solution": "We must have $x=0$ at the $y$-intercepts. \n\nSo, we need to substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the circle and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =64 \\\\ {0}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =64 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =64 \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{64} \\\\ y & =\\pm 8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y$-intercepts occur at the points $(0,-8)$ and $(0,8),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13959190/assets/90fc285151a5f549992e3c40ba6cff89532398808d6194fdf7922108b73646ef.png)",
